# OneWoW Player Wiki

`wiki/` is the **player** documentation surface. It syncs one-way to the GitHub
Wiki tab via `.github/workflows/publish-wiki.yml` (`Andrew-Chen-Wang/github-wiki-action`).
Never instruct editing pages in the GitHub Wiki UI — the next push from `main`
overwrites them.

Engineering Docs (`OneWoW/Docs/`, `ADDON/Docs/`) and code remain the source of
truth. When wiki and Docs disagree, fix the wiki.

## Page mechanics

- **No leading `#` H1** — GitHub Wiki already titles the page from the filename
  (`Bags-Search-Syntax.md` → “Bags Search Syntax”).
- **Flat layout** — all pages in `wiki/` root. Shared chrome only:
  `_Sidebar.md`, `_Footer.md`.
- **Filenames** — use dashes for multi-word titles; keep basenames unique.
- **LF only** — repo-wide; never CRLF.
- **Homepage** — `Home.md` (not `README.md`).

## Related → Sources

Every content page ends with:

```markdown
## Related

* …wiki and in-game pointers…

### Sources

* [path](https://github.com/kellewic/OneWoW_Suite/blob/main/path) — …
```

**Sources must use explicit `blob/main/` URLs.** Relative `../README.md` links are
**not** rewritten correctly for the wiki tab (they become
`github.com/…/OneWoW_Suite/README.md` without `/blob/main/`). Absolute `https://`
links pass through the Action’s preprocess unchanged.

## Content rules

- **Rewrite, don’t paste Docs.** Strip API surfaces, file maps, agent/implementer
  notes, and SV schema. Player example: wiki `Bags-Search-Syntax` vs
  `OneWoW_Bags/Docs/SEARCH_SYNTAX.md`.
- **One feature ≈ one overview page**; long how-tos (search syntax) get their own page.
- **Developers** page stays thin — commentary + links into repo Docs, not a second Docs tree.
- **Do not** document AccountSync or similar non-player package tools on the wiki
  unless product policy explicitly changes.
- Keywords in search docs stay **English-only**; say so when relevant.

## Catalog parity (new feature module)

When adding a public feature load unit, update together:

1. Root `README.md` (catalog table + mermaid if present)
2. `ADDON/README.md` (player overview)
3. `wiki/<Feature>.md` + `_Sidebar.md` (and Home feature table if listed)
4. `OneWoW/Docs/README.md` feature-addons index when contributor Docs exist

## Publish

- Workflow: path-filtered push to `main` on `wiki/**` (+ the workflow file).
- `contents: write`; `disable-empty-commits: true`; action `@v5`.
- Wiki backend must already exist (one-time dummy page in GitHub UI — already done
  for this repo).

## Release notes

`wiki/Release-Notes.md` is the **index** (in-game What’s New “Release notes”
button links here). Full shipped notes live on per-version pages
`wiki/Release-Notes-<TOCVersion>.md` (e.g. `Release-Notes-R6.2608.1105.md`).
Editable source is this repo’s `wiki/`; `publish-wiki.yml` pushes to GitHub’s
wiki repo — never edit the Wiki UI.

**Direction:** always mirror from root `CHANGELOG.md` → `## Current` on the
index. Never draft release-note bullets on the wiki first (changelog pipeline
owns that decision).

**Index shape** (`Release-Notes.md`):

1. `## Current` — in-progress draft body (or empty Draft shell).
2. Shipped versions newest-first — each `## <TOCVersion>` with:
   - One short theme paragraph: `Released <Mon DD, YYYY>. <player themes…>`
   - `[Read full release notes](Release-Notes-<TOCVersion>)`
3. Trailing Related / Sources (Sources keep the `blob/main/` CHANGELOG link).

Do **not** paste full changelog bodies into the index for shipped versions.

**Archive page shape** (`Release-Notes-<TOCVersion>.md`):

- No leading H1 (wiki titles from the filename).
- Leading `- **Release**` / `- **Version**` metadata.
- Full demoted changelog body for that ship.
- Related links back to `[Release notes](Release-Notes)` plus the usual chrome;
  Sources include CHANGELOG + in-game What’s New pointer.

### `## Current` (as you go)

While a release is in progress, keep `## Current` on the **index** in lockstep
with `CHANGELOG.md`:

1. Copy the changelog **body** (everything after `# OneWoW Suite Changelog`,
   excluding that title H1).
2. **Demote headings one level** under `## Current`: changelog `# Addon` →
   `### Addon`, changelog `## Area` → `#### Area`. Preserve `-` bullets, `---`,
   the italic no-changes footer, and nesting.
3. Keep the Current metadata block (Status: Draft) and the trailing Related /
   Sources chrome on the index; leave shipped version summary blocks below
   Current untouched.
4. Sources should keep the explicit `blob/main/` link to `CHANGELOG.md`.

Triggered whenever `onewow-changelog` adds or changes player-facing bullets.

### At CurseForge release

1. **Create** `wiki/Release-Notes-<TOCVersion>.md` from the Current body;
   stamp `- **Release**` / `- **Version**` (TOC `## Version`) at the top;
   add Related / Sources (link back to the index).
2. **Index:** replace Current with an empty Draft shell; insert a new
   `## <TOCVersion>` summary block (newest first, above older summaries) —
   one theme paragraph + `[Read full release notes](Release-Notes-<TOCVersion>)`.
   Author the summary from player themes (do not dump the full changelog).
3. **Reset** root `CHANGELOG.md` to its skeleton (`OneWoW-Changelog.mdc`) when
   the release bot does not already clear it.
4. What’s New highlights reset/rebuild with the next changelog cycle
   (`OneWoW-Changelog.mdc` § What’s New) — not a wiki concern beyond the
   archive step above.
